cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, or quote a number measured in it, please cite it as below."
title: "See the drone, then hit it (SpeckLock)"
abstract: >-
  Two halves of one problem. Detection: find a drone 4-15 pixels across (square root of
  box area) in 720p video by stabilising and stacking three grayscale moments, so that the
  static world cancels and movers leave colour trails. Measured on real, hand-labelled video:
  on a near-static camera a temporal-stack model scores AP 0.895 where a controlled
  single-frame model scores 0.159, with pasted training instances in the temporal arm only;
  on two benchmarks whose cameras move (ARD-MAV, NPS-Drones) the stack does not separate from
  a single frame. Pursuit: close on that drone with camera-only proportional-navigation guidance,
  a four-camera 360-degree ring and a mission FSM — measured closed-loop in NVIDIA Isaac
  Sim. There is no flight test in this repository.
type: software
